ayed since 1982.","The Truth (Lefebvre)"],"17566770":["The Grasshopper is an 1872 oil painting by the French artist Jules Joseph Lefebvre (1836–1911). The painting is in the collection of the National Gallery of Victoria in Melbourne, having been acquired in 2005 through the Felton Bequest.","The Grasshopper (painting)"],"17566948":["Lady Godiva is an 1890 history painting by the French artist Jules Joseph Lefebvre. It depicts the 11th-century Anglo-Saxon noblewoman Lady Godiva riding naked through the streets of Coventry in the English Midlands.","Lady Godiva (Lefebvre)"],"17613629":["The Death of Priam is an 1861 oil on canvas by Jules Lefebvre. He entered it for the Prix de Rome, which it won.","The Death of Priam (Lefebvre)"],"27951257":["Diana Surprised is an 1879 oil painting by Jules Joseph Lefebvre. It depicts Diana and her attendants trying to cover themselves after being surprised while bathing naked.","Diana Surprised"]},"titlesFrom":["fr","P1476","alias:en","alias:fr","aliasFilter:1"]}